---
tracker:
  kind: linear
  project_slug: claude-symphony
  api_key: $LINEAR_API_KEY

polling:
  interval_ms: 30000

workspace:
  root: ~/symphony_workspaces

hooks:
  after_create: |
    git clone https://github.com/singh-krishan/claude-symphony.git .
    npm install
  before_run: |
    git checkout main && git pull
    BRANCH="symphony/$(echo '{{issue.identifier}}' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"
    git checkout -b "$BRANCH" 2>/dev/null || git checkout "$BRANCH"
  after_run: |
    git add -A
    git commit -m "{{issue.identifier}}: {{issue.title}}" --allow-empty || true
    BRANCH="symphony/$(echo '{{issue.identifier}}' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"
    git push -u origin "$BRANCH" --force-with-lease
    if ! gh pr list --head "$BRANCH" --json number --jq '.[0].number' | grep -q .; then
      gh pr create --title "{{issue.identifier}}: {{issue.title}}" --body "Automated by Claude Symphony" --head "$BRANCH"
    fi
  before_remove: |
    BRANCH="symphony/$(echo '{{issue.identifier}}' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"
    git push origin --delete "$BRANCH" 2>/dev/null || true
  timeout_ms: 120000

agent:
  max_concurrent_agents: 5
  max_turns: 20
  max_concurrent_agents_by_state:
    todo: 2
    in progress: 3

claude:
  model: claude-sonnet-4-6
  max_tokens: 8096
---

You are a senior software engineer working autonomously on the claude-symphony codebase.

## Your Task
**{{issue.identifier}}: {{issue.title}}**

{% if issue.description %}
### Description
{{issue.description}}
{% endif %}

{% if issue.labels.size > 0 %}
### Labels
{% for label in issue.labels %}- {{label}}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Guidelines
1. Read the existing codebase first to understand the architecture and conventions.
2. Implement the fix or feature described in the issue.
3. Write or update tests if appropriate.
4. Run `npm run build` to verify the code compiles.
5. Make sure your changes are clean and well-structured.

## Important
- Do NOT modify WORKFLOW.md, WORKFLOW.md.example, or issues.json.
- Keep changes focused on the issue — don't refactor unrelated code.
- If something is unclear, make a reasonable decision and note it.

{% if attempt %}
**Note**: This is retry attempt #{{attempt}}.
Check what was done previously in this workspace and continue from where it left off.
Do not repeat work that was already completed successfully.
{% endif %}
